course: dictionary
lesson: 8674
title: The Seder meal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seder is a special meal and service that Jewish families hold at home. It is held on the first night (or the first two nights) of Passover. Context helps here: «At the Seder the story is told to children, who ask questions about why this night is different.» So a seder is a meal where a story is told and questions are asked.
explain: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival remembering the Exodus from Egypt, with the Seder meal and matzah.» The Exodus is when God freed the Israelites from slavery in Egypt. Put the clues together: the seder is a part of Passover, and it helps families remember that story.
explain: Read the words around the word. «A Passover seder» and «hold a seder» show that families hold one, like a special gathering. A good check is to swap in the word "meal" and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so a seder is a kind of meal.
fact: A seder is held at home on the first night (or first two nights) of Passover.
fact: At a seder, the family reads the story of the Exodus from the Haggadah and eats symbolic foods.
fact: Foods on the seder plate include matzah (flat bread), bitter herbs, salt water and a roasted bone.
fact: The youngest child asks four questions during the seder.
fact: The word «Seder» is often written with a capital S.
exercise: What is a seder? | A type of spring rain | A school trip to a museum | A shop that sells flat bread | *A special meal and service held at home at Passover
exercise: «Passover, or Pesach, is a spring festival remembering the Exodus from Egypt.» In which season is Passover? | Summer | Winter | *Spring | Autumn
exercise: Which food on the seder plate is flat bread? | A roasted bone | *Matzah | Salt water | Bitter herbs
test: At a seder, which child asks four questions? | The grandparents | The oldest child | The visitor | *The youngest child
test: From which book does the family read the story of the Exodus at a seder? | A newspaper | A recipe book | *The Haggadah | A library book
exam: Read: «Jewish life has its own rhythm: Shabbat each week, Passover in spring with the Seder meal, Hanukkah with eight nights of lights.» Which meal is held at Passover? | Matzah alone | Eight nights of lights | A fast for saying sorry | *The Seder meal
